From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tom <tompt@seznam.cz>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 04:17:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: apple_tristar_charger: reject invalid pack
 capacity

Reject successful capacity reads outside 0..100 before using the pack
snapshot. An invalid SOC currently passes the D2355 pack check when
temperature, voltage and current are in range, retaining a higher input
limit. Returning -ERANGE makes the required-telemetry guard withdraw to
the fallback instead.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
index 54bbd0970..9e6381985 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/apple_tristar_charger.c
@@ -374,6 +374,8 @@ static int tristar_read_pack(struct tristar_pack *pack)
 		ret = -ENODEV;
 	if (!ret)
 		ret = power_supply_get_property(battery, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CAPACITY, &val);
+	if (!ret && (val.intval < 0 || val.intval > 100))
+		ret = -ERANGE;
 	if (!ret) {
 		pack->capacity = val.intval;
 		ret = power_supply_get_property(battery, POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TEMP, &val);
